The yellow blocks at rows 45–50 are **two separate 3×3 blocks** at cols 51–53 (rows 45–50, i.e. two stacked) plus a 3×3 at cols 54–56 (rows 48–50). My previous code treated the whole 9-wide region as one block. The code now finds **all** 3×3 uniform blocks of `Y` and moves each by 3 pixels opposite the action direction, handling stacked blocks correctly.

